From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:57:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 491/491] [KV] Capacity figure: the sliding window per request,
 the unsettled batches once

The capacity figure charged every request its sliding-window groups' own
peak: the window plus one whole batch per concurrent step. Those unsettled
tokens fill at most max_in_flight_tokens across all requests, so each request
now pays its window and lookahead, and the pool pays the unsettled batches
once (KVCacheSpec.max_capacity_blocks). The figure takes the larger of this
and the per-request-peak concurrency, so it never drops below the old one.

On DeepSeek V4.1 Flash's TP4 ring (49,483 blocks of 227,840 bytes, 15
window groups) the figure was 8.18 full 1M contexts at 8,192 batched tokens
and 6.21 at 16,384; it is 11.48 and 11.02. The startup check and the
full-sequence admission gate keep one request's own peak, which a lone
prefill reaches (its chunk in flight and its next one).

Tests: the DS4.1 ring at both budgets, the kpool tail's one block, and an
async scheduler run whose real block use stays within the new bound while
one request holds two chunks.
